{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pair of standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided dice is rolled once. The sum of the numbers rolled determines the diameter of a circle. What is the probability that the numerical value of the area of the circle is less than the numerical value of the circle's circumference?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be287cfc64dd90985523555323fec49cccf79d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{36} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{12} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"394\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the circumference to be greater than the area, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b762907122c836f221242a6fc07e23e678cd9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi d &gt; \\pi \\left( \\frac{d}{2} \\right) ^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"108\" height=\"48\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0062e1b0b4aeaab69aaf5044069ffadbec8280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&lt;4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is determined by a sum of two dice, the only possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In order for two dice to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, they must both show a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The probability of this happening is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731f6869a5c488a1a8bba39817cc1591f7815e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />. In order for two dice to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one must show a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other must show a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since this can happen in two ways, the probability of this event occurring is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d91f444e570db06921dc5566771c12aaf88037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{2}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />. The sum of these two probabilities now gives the final answer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bc0d13eb53f9ab392a16fef023ee6592758f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{2}{36} = \\frac{3}{36} = \\frac{1}{12} \\rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6tlqpAcmbz4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6tlqpAcmbz4</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A\">2011 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_P